@title Combat animation timings
@subtitle Four animations, each with a faster and a slower variant to compare

This page cannot play or replay an animation, and it has no sliders. What it gives you is every timing laid out to scale, a faster and a slower variant of each, and the final numbers in a block you can copy into the game. The variants are my own guess at a useful spread: faster is 75% of your timing and slower is 150%. Change them to suit.

kpi Card draw | 280 ms
kpi Damage number | 600 ms
kpi Low-health pulse | 1.2 s
kpi Card discard | 220 ms

## 1. Card draw
The card moves from the deck at the bottom right into the hand, easing out, with a 4 degree tilt that settles flat by the end of the move.

data draw = variant,start,end; Faster (210 ms),0,210; Yours (280 ms),0,280; Slower (420 ms),0,420
chart range draw from=start to=end unit=ms title="Card draw, deck to hand"

## 2. Damage number
It appears on the monster and rises 40 px. It fades during the last 200 ms of the rise. Normal hits are white. Crits are orange and 1.6x bigger.

data dmg = phase,start,end; Faster: rise,0,450; Faster: fade,300,450; Yours: rise,0,600; Yours: fade,400,600; Slower: rise,0,900; Slower: fade,600,900
chart range dmg from=start to=end unit=ms title="Damage number, rise and fade"

table = Hit,Colour,Size; Normal,White,1.0x; Crit,Orange,1.6x

## 3. Low-health warning
The health bar pulses red once every 1.2 s while health is under 25%. It stays gentle: ease the red in and out, do not switch it on and off sharply, and stay far below 3 pulses a second. Offer a reduced-motion setting that holds a steady red instead.

table = Variant,Cycle,Pulses per second; Faster,0.9 s,1.1; Yours,1.2 s,0.8; Slower,1.8 s,0.6

!! Do not speed this up past about 3 pulses a second, and avoid large bright flashes. That is the range that can trigger people who are sensitive to flicker.

## 4. Card discard
The card shrinks to 60% of its size and fades out together, in 220 ms.

data discard = variant,start,end; Faster (165 ms),0,165; Yours (220 ms),0,220; Slower (330 ms),0,330
chart range discard from=start to=end unit=ms title="Card discard, shrink and fade"

## Test cards
Made-up cards for trying each animation.

table = Card,Effect,Shows; Cinder Strike,6 damage,Damage number (normal and crit); Guard Up,Block 5,Draw and discard; Lucky Find,Draw 2,Two card draws in a row

## Compare all variants
table = Animation,Faster,Yours,Slower; Card draw,210 ms,280 ms,420 ms; Damage number total,450 ms,600 ms,900 ms; Damage number fade,150 ms,200 ms,300 ms; Low-health pulse,0.9 s,1.2 s,1.8 s; Card discard,165 ms,220 ms,330 ms

## Numbers to copy
These are your current timings. Edit them here as you settle, then paste into the game.

```json
{
  "cardDraw":     { "durationMs": 280, "easing": "ease-out", "tiltDeg": 4 },
  "damageNumber": { "durationMs": 600, "risePx": 40, "fadeMs": 200, "critScale": 1.6, "normalColor": "white", "critColor": "orange" },
  "lowHealth":    { "thresholdPercent": 25, "pulseCycleMs": 1200, "color": "red" },
  "cardDiscard":  { "durationMs": 220, "scaleTo": 0.6, "fade": true }
}
```
